language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Just forgotten: find the account number x, a permutation of the digits 0 to n-1, that agrees with each given set in exactly the stated number of positions.
$ number of sets, from the instance
given sets_dim1 : int
$ number of digits n, from the instance
given sets_dim2 : int
$ the sets of digits that Joe tried, one per row
given sets : matrix indexed by [int(1..sets_dim1), int(1..sets_dim2)] of int
$ how many digits of each set are in their correct position
given num_correct_digits : int
$ the account number: x[p] is the digit at position p, positions counted from 1 in the model and 0 in the output
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..sets_dim2)] of int(0..sets_dim2-1)
such that
$ the account number uses each digit from 0 to n-1 exactly once
allDiff(x),
$ each tried set has exactly num_correct_digits digits in the same position as the account number
forAll k : int(1..sets_dim1) . ((sum p : int(1..sets_dim2) . toInt(x[p] = sets[k,p])) = num_correct_digits)
